title: 3-6 words, the thing being taught. subtitle: one short line, the promise of the clip.
{{- end}}

{{define "user" -}}
{{if .Script -}}
THE CREATOR HAS WRITTEN THE NARRATION. These are their words and they are not yours to improve:

---
{{.Script}}
---

Your job is direction, not writing. Split that script into beats and stage each one.

The narration fields, joined together in order, must contain EXACTLY the words above — same words, same order, nothing added, nothing dropped, nothing reworded. You may split a sentence across two beats and you may put a sentence boundary wherever a shot should change. You may not tighten a line, fix its grammar, swap a synonym, or add a transition. This is checked word by word and a single changed word fails the whole plan.

Everything else is yours: the headings, the shots, the figures, the captions, the emphasis. The heading is NOT the narration — it is the short line on screen that the narration is talking around, so write one that adds to the sentence rather than repeating it.

Aim for about {{.WordsPerBeat}} words of narration per beat, which is roughly {{.SuggestBeats}} beats for this script. A beat may be as short as {{.MinWordsPerBeat}} words and no longer than {{.MaxWordsPerBeat}}, so cut the script wherever that lands naturally.

{{if .Prompt}}What the clip is for, in the creator's words: {{.Prompt}}
{{end}}
{{- else -}}
Direct a clip about:

{{.Prompt}}

Write the narration and stage it. Structure the clip as {{.MinBeats}} to {{.MaxBeats}} beats — about {{.SuggestBeats}} is right for this runtime — with roughly {{.WordsPerBeat}} words of narration each.

LENGTH IS A HARD REQUIREMENT. The narration across all beats must total between {{.MinWords}} and {{.MaxWords}} words — aim for {{.TargetWords}}. The shots are timed to the voice, so narration that comes in short is half a video.

Give it an arc: open by naming what the viewer is dealing with, turn on the idea, close on what they can now do.
{{- end}}
{{if .Title}}
Use exactly this title: {{.Title}}
{{end}}
{{if .Facts}}
